+
+
+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* may also declare a default value for an argument. This is mostly
+useful for a new hookimpl that wants to accept an argument which an older
+version of the hookspec does not provide yet.
+
+The value a hookimpl receives for such an argument is chosen in this order:
+
+1. The value passed by the hook call.
+2. The hookspec's default value for the argument.
+3. The hookimpl's own default value.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="impl-default"):
+        # new_arg is the value passed by the caller, or the hookspec default,
+        # or "impl-default" when the hookspec doesn't know about new_arg.
+        ...
+
+This applies to plain hookimpls as well as to wrappers and old-style
+hookwrappers.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+   Previously the hookimpl's default value was always used, even when the hook
+   call passed an explicit value.
 
 
